## Spec B5 (docs/specs/stdlib/async.spec.md): a class that
## `include`s `Future` but omits the required `type Output = T`
## binding should be rejected by the typeck. The validation pass
## that enforces this does not yet exist (sub-phase 1 ships the
## surface only); the pin test using this fixture is `#[ignore]`d
## until the validator lands.

class BadFuture
  include Future

  def var poll(cx: &var Context) -> Poll[Int]
    Poll.Ready(0)
  end
end

def main
  let _f = BadFuture.new
  puts "should-not-compile"
end
